{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The [struct","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"] struct represents a read-write lock. A read-write"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lock can be used for protecting data that some portions of code only","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read from, while others also write. In such situations it is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"desirable that several readers can read at once, whereas of course"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"only one writer may write at a time.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StaticRWLockProtocol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PointerWrapper","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib14PointerWrapperP","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Take a look at the following example:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["  GStaticRWLock rwlock = G_STATIC_RW_LOCK_INIT;","  GPtrArray *array;","","  gpointer","  my_array_get (guint index)","  {","    gpointer retval = NULL;","","    if (!array)","      return NULL;","","    g_static_rw_lock_reader_lock (&rwlock);","    if (index < array->len)","      retval = g_ptr_array_index (array, index);","    g_static_rw_lock_reader_unlock (&rwlock);","","    return retval;","  }","","  void","  my_array_set (guint index, gpointer data)","  {","    g_static_rw_lock_writer_lock (&rwlock);","","    if (!array)","      array = g_ptr_array_new ();","","    if (index >= array->len)","      g_ptr_array_set_size (array, index + 1);","    g_ptr_array_index (array, index) = data;","","    g_static_rw_lock_writer_unlock (&rwlock);","  }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This example shows an array which can be accessed by many readers"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"my_array_get()"},{"text":" function) simultaneously, whereas the writers","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the "},{"code":"my_array_set()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function) will only be allowed once at a time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and only if no readers currently access the array. This is because","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of the potentially dangerous resizing of the array. Using these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"functions is fully multi-thread safe now.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most of the time, writers should have precedence over readers. That","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"means, for this implementation, that as soon as a writer wants to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"lock the data, no other reader is allowed to lock the data, whereas,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of course, the readers that already have locked the data are allowed"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to finish their operation. As soon as the last reader unlocks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"data, the writer will lock it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Even though [struct"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock"},{"text":"] is not opaque, it should only be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"with the following functions."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_rw_lock_*"},{"text":" functions can be used even if","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.init"},{"type":"text","text":"] has not been called. Then they do nothing, apart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_rw_lock_*_trylock"},{"type":"text","text":", which does nothing but returning true."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A read-write lock has a higher overhead than a mutex. For example, both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StaticRWLock.reader_lock"},{"text":"] and [method","type":"text"},{"code":"StaticRWLock.reader_unlock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] have"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to lock and unlock a [struct","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex"},{"text":"], so it takes at least twice the time","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to lock and unlock a [struct"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"] that it does to lock and unlock a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[struct","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex"},{"text":"]. So only data structures that are accessed by multiple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"readers, and which keep the lock for a considerable time justify a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[struct","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"]. The above example most probably would fare better with a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[struct","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol exposes the methods and properties of an underlying "},{"code":"GStaticRWLock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"The default implementation of these can be found in the protocol extension below."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a concrete class that implements these methods and properties, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Alternatively, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockRef","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a lighweight, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unowned"},{"type":"text","text":" reference if you already have an instance you just want to use."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol"]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/free()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/init_()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/readerLock()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/readerTrylock()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/readerUnlock()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/writerLock()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/writerTrylock()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/writerUnlock()"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper"],"kind":"relationships"},{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformingTypes","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockRef"],"title":"Conforming Types"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StaticRWLockProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib20StaticRWLockProtocolP","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StaticRWLockProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","title":"StaticRWLockProtocol","role":"symbol"},"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLock":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StaticRWLock","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"StaticRWLock","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The [struct"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"] struct represents a read-write lock. A read-write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lock can be used for protecting data that some portions of code only"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read from, while others also write. In such situations it is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"desirable that several readers can read at once, whereas of course"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only one writer may write at a time."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlock","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StaticRWLock"}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/Mutex":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex"},{"type":"text","text":" struct is an opaque data structure to represent a mutex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(mutual exclusion). It can be used to protect data against shared","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Mutex","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Mutex","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"Mutex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/mutex"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticMutex":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticmutex","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StaticMutex"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex","title":"StaticMutex","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticMutex"},{"type":"text","text":" works like a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Mutex"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StaticMutex","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockProtocol/readerLock()":{"title":"readerLock()","deprecated":true,"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/readerLock()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"readerLock","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Locks "},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for reading. There may be unlimited concurrent locks for"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reading of a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" at the same time.  If ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"text":" is already","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"locked for writing by another thread or if another thread is already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"waiting to lock "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":" for writing, this function will block until"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"text":" is unlocked by the other writing thread and no other writing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"threads want to lock ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"text":". This lock has to be unlocked by","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"g_static_rw_lock_reader_unlock()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol\/readerlock()"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockProtocol/readerUnlock()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlocks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":". If a thread waits to lock "},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for writing and all"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"locks for reading have been unlocked, the waiting thread is woken up","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and can lock ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"text":" for writing.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol\/readerunlock()","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/readerUnlock()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"readerUnlock","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"deprecated":true,"kind":"symbol","title":"readerUnlock()","type":"topic"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockProtocol/writerUnlock()":{"title":"writerUnlock()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol\/writerunlock()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"writerUnlock","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/writerUnlock()","deprecated":true,"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlocks "},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If a thread is waiting to lock "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":" for writing and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"all locks for reading have been unlocked, the waiting thread is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"woken up and can lock ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":" for writing. If no thread is waiting to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lock ","type":"text"},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for writing, and some thread or threads are waiting to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"lock ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":" for reading, the waiting threads are woken up and can"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"lock "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":" for reading."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockProtocol/init_()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"init_"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"symbol","deprecated":true,"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" must be initialized with this function before it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be used. Alternatively you can initialize it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G_STATIC_RW_LOCK_INIT"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"init_()","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/init_()","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol\/init_()","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockProtocol/free()":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Releases all resources allocated to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"free()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/free()","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol\/free()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"free"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"deprecated":true},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/PointerWrapper":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PointerWrapper"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Protocol for GLib types that wrap pointers.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/pointerwrapper","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PointerWrapper","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PointerWrapper","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockProtocol/writerTrylock()":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol\/writertrylock()","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/writerTrylock()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries to lock "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":" for writing. If "},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is already locked (for"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"either reading or writing) by another thread, it immediately returns"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Otherwise it locks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"text":" for writing and returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":". This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lock has to be unlocked by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_rw_lock_writer_unlock()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"deprecated":true,"title":"writerTrylock()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writerTrylock","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockProtocol":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StaticRWLockProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"StaticRWLockProtocol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StaticRWLockProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The [struct"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLock"},{"text":"] struct represents a read-write lock. A read-write","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lock can be used for protecting data that some portions of code only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"read from, while others also write. In such situations it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"desirable that several readers can read at once, whereas of course"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"only one writer may write at a time.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockProtocol/writerLock()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Locks ","type":"text"},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for writing. If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lock"},{"type":"text","text":" is already locked for writing or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reading by other threads, this function will block until ","type":"text"},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"completely unlocked and then lock "},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for writing. While this"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"functions waits to lock ","type":"text"},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", no other thread can lock "},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reading. When "},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is locked for writing, no other thread can lock"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"lock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (neither for reading nor writing). This lock has to be","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"unlocked by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_static_rw_lock_writer_unlock()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"writerLock()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StaticRWLockProtocol\/writerLock()","role":"symbol","deprecated":true,"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/staticrwlockprotocol\/writerlock()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"writerLock"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/StaticRWLockRef":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StaticRWLockRef"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The [struct","type":"tex